  "ingredients": [
    "2 tablespoon fresh parsley (chopped)",
    "1 medium spaghetti squash",
    "2 tablespoon olive oil",
    "1/2 medium onion (diced)",
    "16 ounce breakfast sausage",
    "16 ounce ground beef (80/20)",
    "1 tablespoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "24 ounce low-carb tomato sauce (like Rao's)",
    "20 ounce ricotta cheese",
    "2 large egg",
    "3/4 cup grated parmesan cheese",
    "2 tablespoon fresh basil (chopped)",
    "1/2 teaspoon salt",
    "1/2 teaspoon pepper",
    "8 ounce fresh mozzarella cheese (sliced)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 400F.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carefully split the spaghetti squash in half lengthwise and scoop out the seeds. Drizzle with olive oil and sprinkle with salt and pepper.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast for 35-45 minutes or until the squash is tender and easily shreds with a fork. Using a fork produces spaghetti-like strands. Remove from the skin into a bowl and set aside. If there’s any visible liquid, drain or pat dry.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the squash roasts, heat the remaining tablespoon of olive oil in a large skillet. Add the diced onion, sausage, ground beef and garlic.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook the meat thoroughly and drain any rendered fat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the marinara sauce to the meat mixture and bring to a boil. Reduce the heat and simmer the sauce for about 15 minutes or until thick and most of the liquid has been reduced.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the meat simmers combine the ricotta cheese, Parmesan cheese, eggs, basil, salt, and pepper in a medium-sized bowl and set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "When squash is done, remove from oven and reduce oven temp to 350F. Lightly grease a 2.5 quart casserole dish.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-08.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Begin with spaghetti squash, adding half the strands (about 2 cups) to the bottom of the dish and pressing into a flat layer.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-09.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Top with half the ricotta mixture and spread out evenly.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add a layer of half the meat sauce, followed by a layer of half the mozzarella cheese. Repeat all of the layers again, starting over with another layer of squash.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sprinkle the casserole with the remaining 1/4 cup of Parmesan cheese and chopped parsley.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole-13.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes. Remove the foil and bake another 20 – 30 minutes or until bubbly and golden brown. Let rest for at least 15 minutes before serving.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/spaghetti-squash-lasagna-casserole/#wprm-recipe-52453-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
